.TH HD-MESSAGE 1 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-message \- a message box for the HyprDebian desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-message
.RI < message.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-message
shows a message in the middle of the screen, with a title, a text and a row
of buttons, chosen from with the keyboard, and prints the value of the button
chosen on stdout.
It takes no arguments; it reads the message as JSON from stdin.
.PP
It draws on a wlr-layer-shell surface over the whole output, so it needs a
Wayland compositor with wlr-layer-shell, such as Hyprland.
The namespace of the surface is
.BR hd-message .
The message box has the keyboard to itself while it is open.
Only one
.B hd-message
is open at a time: another one exits at once with 1.
.SH THE MESSAGE
.nf
{
    "title": "Reboot system?",
    "text": "The new kernel is used after a reboot.\enUnsaved work is lost.",
    "width": 600,
    "buttons": [
        {"label": "Later", "value": "later"},
        {"label": "Reboot", "value": "reboot", "icon": "/usr/share/icons/reboot.svg"}
    ],
    "default": "later"
}
.fi
.TP
.B title
Optional: a line of text at the top, in the big font, with a divider under it.
.TP
.B text
Optional: the message, in the normal font.
It is wrapped at the spaces to the width of the box; a word that is wider
than the box on its own is broken between characters.
A newline (\e\&n) starts a new line, an empty line between two newlines.
.TP
.B width
Optional: the width of the box, in logical pixels (a number) or as a
percentage of the output (a string such as \(dq50%\(dq).
Without it, the box is as wide as the title, the text and the buttons need,
but the text wraps at half the width of the output.
The box is as high as its content needs.
It is never larger than the output; text that does not fit is cut off.
.TP
.B buttons
The buttons, from left to right; at least one.
All buttons are as wide as the widest.
Each is an object with:
.RS
.TP
.B label
The text shown.
.TP
.B value
Optional: what
.B hd-message
prints when the button is chosen; the label when there is none.
.TP
.B icon
Optional: the path of a PNG or SVG
.RB ( .svg " or " .svgz )
image, shown left of the label at the
.B icon_size
of the theme.
An icon that cannot be loaded is left out, with a message on stderr.
.RE
.TP
.B default
Optional: the value of the button selected at the start; the first button
when there is none.
.PP
Other members are ignored.
.PP
The Font Awesome glyphs of the Nerd Font of
.BR hd-fonts ,
such as \e\&uf00c (a check mark) and \e\&uf00d (a cross), can be written as
escapes in the title, the text and a label.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right ", " Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Select the previous or next button.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
Select the first or the last button.
.TP
.B Enter
Choose the selected button.
.TP
.BR Escape ", " q
Close the message box without a choice. q is the key with the letter q in the
keyboard layout, with or without Shift.
.PP
A key that is held repeats at the rate and after the delay of the compositor,
.B input:repeat_rate
and
.B input:repeat_delay
in Hyprland.
.SH THE THEME
.B hd-message
draws the message in the
.B hd-theme
of the configuration of the user,
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
or, when that has none, of the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ;
when neither has it, it uses defaults of its own, and run as root it only
reads the configuration of the system.
.BR hd-theme (1)
sets the key when a theme is selected.
The theme gives the font, its
.B font-size-big
for the title and its
.B font-size-normal
for the text and the buttons, the colours
.B dark
(the background, at
.BR opacity ),
.B light
(the text),
.B normal
(the selected button, the outline of the other buttons and the divider) and
.B highlight
(the border), the
.B border
width, the corner
.B radius
and the
.BR icon_size .
The font sizes are in points, like in the other programs of the theme;
.B hd-message
draws them at 4/3 logical pixels per point.
The border, the radius and the icon size are in logical pixels.
All these sizes are multiplied by the factor of the key
.B hd-display
of the configuration of the system, as
.B hd-theme \-\-apply
does for the other programs; see
.B SCALING
in
.BR hd-theme (7).
The scale of the monitor decides how large that is on the screen.
A setting that is missing has its default; when the file cannot be read, the
whole theme has.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A button was chosen; its value is on stdout.
.TP
.B 1
The message box was closed without a choice, or another
.B hd-message
is open.
.TP
.B 2
An error: arguments, invalid JSON on stdin, a message without buttons, a
default that is not the value of a button, or no Wayland compositor with
wlr-layer-shell.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The theme of the user, in
.BR hd-theme .
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The theme of the system, in
.BR hd-theme ,
when the user has none.
.TP
.IR /run/user/ UID /hd-message.lock
The lock that keeps a second
.B hd-message
from opening.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask before a reboot, with No selected:
.PP
.nf
message=\(aq{"title": "Reboot system?", "text": "Unsaved work is lost.",
  "buttons": [{"label": "No"}, {"label": "Yes"}], "default": "No"}\(aq
if [[ "$(echo "$message" | hd-message)" == "Yes" ]]; then
    hd-reboot
fi
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-menu (1),
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-theme (1),
.BR hd-config (7)
